    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35849" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">petrōsus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		1. petra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of rocks</i>, <i>rocky</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 31, 50, § 96</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">petrōsa</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n., <i>rocky
				places</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maritima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 8, 29, § 46</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Laps. Virg. 7, 29</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliud cecidit super petrosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Marc. 4, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Matt. 13, 5</span></i>.</div>
